From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:01:06 +0200
Subject: media: gc2145: Manage power with runtime PM

The subdev .s_power operation is deprecated and bridges are moving away
from calling it, which leaves the sensor powered down when its controls
and its stream are set up. Switch to runtime PM as
Documentation/driver-api/media/camera-sensor.rst requires.

The chip id read moves to probe, where the device is powered explicitly
for it, so that a resume no longer has to identify the part. Mode setup
moves out of the power-on path and into stream start, which is where it
belongs anyway and where the firmware load has a bound v4l2_device to
take its parent from. Controls now check the runtime PM state instead of
a private flag, and the ones that only update driver state are handled
before that check so they work while the sensor is suspended.

The system sleep handlers go away with it: the pipeline is responsible
for stopping the stream over a suspend, and forcing the runtime state is
enough to drop the rails.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
